From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:47:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): opt-in subagent results that reach a running
 turn

sessions.mid_turn_subagent_results (default false): a background
delegate_task result admitted while its local session's turn runs is
transferred to that turn, like prompt.steer_queued, and rides the
turn's next tool result instead of waiting behind the turn. It is not
wrapped as a user steer, and no running tool is interrupted. When no
tool result takes it, the claim's settlement puts it back in its queue
place, where it runs or is noted as before. Only a result dispatched
from the same conversation is handed over.
